    "description": "Count an incomplete review as a failed eval repeat\n\n## The defect\n\n`pr-review eval` counted a repeat as failed only when the review run exited nonzero or threw. A review whose queries fail ends with the verdict `incomplete` and exits 0, by design. The eval then scored that repeat as a valid run with zero findings: recall 0 and precision null. So `--write-baseline` wrote a wrong baseline, and the gate compared against wrong values. In one real run, 8 of 12 repeats were incomplete, and the eval still wrote the baseline.\n\n## The fix\n\n`src/eval/run.ts` now sends a repeat whose record has the verdict `incomplete` through the existing failed-repeat path. The repeat goes into `failed_repeats` with null metrics. It stops `--write-baseline`, and the eval exits 1. The error starts with \"The review was incomplete.\" and then gives each distinct entry of `cost.errors` in the record, as `stage: message`.\n\nThe README now says that an incomplete review is a failed repeat. It also says that a failed judge query is not a failed repeat.\n\n## The tests\n\nThe fake SDK client of `test/eval-cli.test.ts` gets a `reviewerFailure` option. In the runs that it names, every reviewer query throws with a given message. Two new tests use it:\n\n- \"lists a repeat whose review is incomplete as a failed repeat with the reason, and exits 1\". The fake throws \"You've hit your session limit\". The test checks the exit code, `failed_repeats`, the error text and the null metrics.\n- \"leaves the baseline unchanged when one review of two is incomplete\". The second review is complete, so the means are not null. Before the fix, the eval wrote the baseline. Now the file does not change, and the eval exits 1.\n\nBoth tests failed before the fix. `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01UKXoH72K6RLXNCGUFmHPfP",
